{
  "dom_id": "step-q154703",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=5,$ then $y=$",
  "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=3-\\frac{2}{3}y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-\\frac{2}{3}y| & =5 \\\\ 3-\\frac{2}{3}y & =5 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3}y & =2 \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3}y) & =(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (2) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{3}{2}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{2}{3}}y) & =-\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ y & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|3-\\frac{2}{3}y|=-(3-\\frac{2}{3}y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-\\frac{2}{3}y| & =5 \\\\ -(3-\\frac{2}{3}y) & =5 \\\\ -3+\\frac{2}{3}y & =5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\frac{3}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y & =8 \\\\ (\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}y) & =(\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (8) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{3}{2}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{2}{3}}y) & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\ y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-3$ and $y=12.$",
